# Store text with Unix line endings; the Windows-run scripts write CRLF in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Fuse maps and Lattice netlist files keep their exact bytes, CRLF line ends included: the
# build checks compare them byte for byte, and a JEDEC file's transmission checksum
# counts every byte. -text keeps them readable in diffs.
*.jed -text
*.laf -text
*.ppn -text
*.par -text
*.bin binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
